  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a free body diagram shown in the figure, the four forces are applied in the &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&#39; and &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>&#39; directions. What additional force must be applied and at what angle with positive <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis so that the net acceleration of body is zero?</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0065_be5d8062cf40.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 201px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>135</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let additional force required be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>.</p><p>Vector sum of the four forces and additional force.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Force required to make net acceleration&nbsp;zero</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Therefore, the required force is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>Angle with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>component</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>component</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}